From: Ryan Chen <rchen14b@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: airoha: add AN7581 CPU PLL fallback

Based on the PM-domain part of community commit 4b786a7dc7.
Q1000K reports CPUFreq ->get() failed when vendor firmware returns no usable clock rate.
Retain SMC when it supplies a valid rate; opt in to the PLL fallback only
on Q1000K. Use the existing chip-SCU syscon instead of claiming its MMIO
resource twice. Quiesce the shared CPU clock domain during transitions,
preserve unrelated bits, validate readback and restrict levels to 500..1200 MHz.
Do not change CPUFreq OPP attachment, voltage settings or Kconfig.

Source: https://github.com/OpenWRT-fanboy/OpenW1700k/commit/4b786a7dc71118e91f092ffa9f428145d992fb00

